# Cloudflare Pages — cache policy to prevent stale-chunk crashes
#
# Problem:  after a deploy, chunk filenames change (they're hash-fingerprinted),
# but if browsers still serve index.html from cache, it references the OLD
# chunk names → ChunkLoadError → "Something went wrong" on every page except
# the one whose chunk happened to still be warm.
#
# Fix:  tell the browser/CDN to always re-validate index.html, but cache the
# hashed assets aggressively (their filename changes on every deploy so
# "immutable" is safe — different content = different URL).

# Never cache the HTML entry point — always re-fetch to get latest chunk refs.
#
# IMPORTANT (BUG-2026-05-28-005): this MUST be `/*`, not `/`. Every SPA route
# (/dashboard, /production/fab-cut, /sales/:id, …) is served the index.html
# body by Cloudflare's SPA fallback, but the URL is the route path — so a rule
# scoped to `/` or `/index.html` never matches them and those HTML responses
# fell back to Cloudflare's default cacheability. Browsers then cached
# /dashboard's HTML, kept pointing at OLD hashed asset names, and after a
# deploy that rotated the CSS/JS hash the page rendered fully unstyled /
# ChunkLoadError. `/*` covers every route; the more-specific `/assets/*` rule
# below overrides Cache-Control back to immutable for fingerprinted assets.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
  Pragma: no-cache
  Expires: 0
  # TEMPORARY diagnostic (2026-07-16) — REMOVE once the route-transition block
  # is root-caused. Chrome refuses `new Profiler()` (the JS Self-Profiling API)
  # without this header, which is the only reason the /invoices "jank" hunt had
  # to guess. It grants nothing else: a page may only profile its OWN
  # same-origin scripts, and the header is inert unless our code calls Profiler.
  #
  # Needed on PROD specifically: staging runs byte-identical src with the same
  # ~200-row data and blocks 0ms, while prod blocks ~150-340ms on every route
  # change — so the cause only reproduces here.
  Document-Policy: js-profiling

# Hashed assets (Vite fingerprints every chunk + stylesheet) — safe to cache
# forever. `immutable` tells the browser it won't change, skip conditional
# revalidation. One-year max-age. More specific than `/*` above, so this
# Cache-Control wins for /assets/* requests.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Static public files (no hash) — short cache with must-revalidate so a new
# favicon/icon still propagates within minutes.
/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate

/icons.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate

/pdf.worker.min.mjs
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
